WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:04.375
Hello, everyone! I'm Mr. Daniel. Welcome to Online Intermediate.

2
00:00:04.675 --> 00:00:07.609
Hi! I'm Nita. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:07.909 --> 00:00:13.185
Unit twenty: Making a Difference. In this unit, you will talk about volunteering and helping the community.

4
00:00:14.183 --> 00:00:15.033
fundraiser.

5
00:00:15.733 --> 00:00:19.045
fundraiser means an event to collect money for a good cause.

6
00:00:19.345 --> 00:00:22.297
The school held a fundraiser for the flood victims.

7
00:00:22.997 --> 00:00:25.208
Your turn. Say: fundraiser.

8
00:00:27.908 --> 00:00:28.932
fundraiser.

9
00:00:29.917 --> 00:00:31.231
community project.

10
00:00:31.931 --> 00:00:35.928
community project means work done by local people to improve their area.

11
00:00:36.228 --> 00:00:39.261
Our community project built a new library.

12
00:00:39.961 --> 00:00:42.566
Your turn. Say: community project.

13
00:00:45.266 --> 00:00:46.569
community project.

14
00:00:47.583 --> 00:00:48.689
non-profit.

15
00:00:49.389 --> 00:00:54.535
non-profit means an organisation that uses its money to help people, not to make profit.

16
00:00:54.835 --> 00:00:57.751
She works for a non-profit that teaches girls to code.

17
00:00:58.451 --> 00:01:00.616
Your turn. Say: non-profit.

18
00:01:03.316 --> 00:01:04.747
non-profit.

19
00:01:05.750 --> 00:01:06.948
social cause.

20
00:01:07.648 --> 00:01:11.540
social cause means a problem in society that people try to solve.

21
00:01:11.840 --> 00:01:14.757
Education for all is a social cause close to my heart.

22
00:01:15.457 --> 00:01:18.028
Your turn. Say: social cause.

23
00:01:20.728 --> 00:01:21.950
social cause.

24
00:01:22.950 --> 00:01:23.789
campaign.

25
00:01:24.489 --> 00:01:27.905
campaign means a planned series of activities to achieve a goal.

26
00:01:28.205 --> 00:01:30.622
The campaign encouraged people to give blood.

27
00:01:31.322 --> 00:01:33.487
Your turn. Say: campaign.

28
00:01:36.187 --> 00:01:37.281
campaign.

29
00:01:38.283 --> 00:01:39.459
donation box.

30
00:01:40.159 --> 00:01:44.422
donation box means a box where people put money or items to give.

31
00:01:44.722 --> 00:01:47.023
Please put coins in the donation box.

32
00:01:47.723 --> 00:01:50.236
Your turn. Say: donation box.

33
00:01:52.936 --> 00:01:54.356
donation box.

34
00:01:55.350 --> 00:01:56.177
good deed.

35
00:01:56.877 --> 00:01:59.678
good deed means a kind action that helps someone.

36
00:01:59.978 --> 00:02:03.359
Helping an old man cross the road was her good deed for the day.

37
00:02:04.059 --> 00:02:06.363
Your turn. Say: good deed.

38
00:02:09.063 --> 00:02:09.959
good deed.

39
00:02:10.950 --> 00:02:11.847
helping hand.

40
00:02:12.547 --> 00:02:14.685
helping hand means help or support.

41
00:02:14.985 --> 00:02:17.264
Thank you for giving me a helping hand with the move.

42
00:02:17.964 --> 00:02:20.210
Your turn. Say: helping hand.

43
00:02:22.910 --> 00:02:24.073
helping hand.

44
00:02:25.083 --> 00:02:27.118
Now let's listen to a conversation.

45
00:02:27.418 --> 00:02:29.591
Nita, I heard you joined a non-profit.

46
00:02:30.883 --> 00:02:36.090
Yes! Bright Futures, which teaches English in villages, needed volunteers.

47
00:02:37.383 --> 00:02:39.583
That's wonderful. What do you do there?

48
00:02:40.883 --> 00:02:44.206
I help with a community project, which started last year.

49
00:02:45.517 --> 00:02:47.284
Are you organising any events?

50
00:02:48.583 --> 00:02:52.324
We're having a fundraiser in May, which my friends are helping with.

51
00:02:53.617 --> 00:02:56.951
Grammar focus: Non-defining relative clauses.

52
00:02:57.251 --> 00:03:00.981
Non-defining relative clauses add extra information about a noun.

53
00:03:01.281 --> 00:03:03.768
We put commas around them, and we never use that.

54
00:03:04.068 --> 00:03:08.482
For example: The fundraiser, which was in May, raised two thousand dollars.

55
00:03:08.782 --> 00:03:13.383
Non-defining clauses add extra information, so they use commas and never use that.

56
00:03:14.383 --> 00:03:17.291
Now read and listen. Small Acts, Big Impact.

57
00:03:17.591 --> 00:03:21.019
Sophea, who is twenty-two, started a reading campaign in her village.

58
00:03:22.317 --> 00:03:26.882
She placed a donation box at the market, where people could leave old books.

59
00:03:28.183 --> 00:03:31.425
Within a month, she had collected over five hundred books.

60
00:03:32.717 --> 00:03:36.632
The project, which began with one good deed, now has thirty volunteers.

61
00:03:37.917 --> 00:03:41.193
Sophea says that everyone can lend a helping hand in some way.

62
00:03:42.483 --> 00:03:44.915
Quiz time! Choose the correct answer.

63
00:03:45.215 --> 00:03:47.946
An event to collect money for a good cause is a blank.

64
00:03:48.246 --> 00:03:51.830
A, fundraiser. B, good deed. C, donation box.

65
00:03:55.817 --> 00:03:57.700
The answer is A: fundraiser.

66
00:03:59.217 --> 00:04:01.971
My brother, blank lives in Tokyo, is an engineer.

67
00:04:02.271 --> 00:04:04.949
A, which. B, who. C, where.

68
00:04:08.950 --> 00:04:10.555
The answer is B: who.

69
00:04:12.050 --> 00:04:14.955
The library, blank opened last year, is very popular.

70
00:04:15.255 --> 00:04:18.084
A, who. B, that. C, which.

71
00:04:22.083 --> 00:04:23.595
The answer is C: which.

72
00:04:25.083 --> 00:04:27.570
A kind action that helps someone is a blank.

73
00:04:27.870 --> 00:04:31.675
A, campaign. B, good deed. C, non-profit.

74
00:04:35.683 --> 00:04:37.845
The answer is B: good deed.

75
00:04:39.350 --> 00:04:43.254
According to the text, how many books did Sophea collect in a month?

76
00:04:43.554 --> 00:04:47.021
A, fifty. B, over five hundred. C, thirty.

77
00:04:51.017 --> 00:04:53.225
The answer is B: over five hundred.

78
00:04:54.717 --> 00:04:58.634
Now it's your turn to speak. Which social cause is important to you, and why?

79
00:05:03.934 --> 00:05:10.172
Education, which changes lives, is the cause I care about most, so I help children read.

80
00:05:10.472 --> 00:05:12.111
Excellent answer, Nita!

81
00:05:13.117 --> 00:05:17.685
Great work today! You learned eight new words and non-defining relative clauses.

82
00:05:17.985 --> 00:05:21.217
Today's value is community. Help the people in your town.

83
00:05:21.517 --> 00:05:23.949
See you in Unit twenty-one. Goodbye!

84
00:05:24.249 --> 00:05:26.960
Thank you, Mr. Daniel! Bye, everyone!

